      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yuki3/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yuki3/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yuki3/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yuki3/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yuki3/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yuki3/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yuki3/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/yuki3/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "created_at": "2017-11-17T13:30:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-11-17T13:30:58Z",
    "body": "Blink's implementation is still far from the ideal state, but I can implement something so that `crossOriginWindow.then` returns `undefined`.  However, I have a concern.\r\n\r\nIf we add `then` to [HTML 7.2.3.3 CrossOriginGetOwnPropertyHelper](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#crossorigingetownpropertyhelper-(-o,-p-)), then `then` has a priority over [7.2.3.1 CrossOriginProperties](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#crossoriginproperties-(-o-)), right?  IIUC, it shadows a child browsing context with the name \"then\".\r\n\r\nShould we deprioritize `then`?  `@@toStringTag`, etc. are probably okay because they're symbols.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/dom/issues/comments/345244266/reactions",
